{"id":"000VVQ","title":"Tenth Sandwich","author":"LittleNightmaresLady","solvedCount":0,"difficulty":5,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-04T23:44:39+00:00","posted":"Gestern, 19:14 Uhr","rules":"Fixed some things.\n\nRules:\n\n-Normal sudoku rules apply.\n\n-Each box, row and column has 2 \"crusts\". In each row and column, the digits in the crusts differ by at least 5. Outside clues give the sum of the digits between the two crusts. The crusts can't touch each other orthogonally, but can touch diagonally. The red cage is not a crust. For clarification, ? is any number from 0 to 9, E means even, and O means odd.\n\n-Divide each grey line into contiguous, non-overlapping groups that sum to 10. Digits may repeat on a line, if allowed by other rules. The different colored line is to indicate that they are different lines.\n\n-A cell with a grey circle contains an odd digit, and a cell with a grey square contains an even digit. An inequality sign points towards the smaller digit.\n\nLinks:\n\nF-puzzles\n\nCTC","solutionCode":"Row 4","tags":["Sudoku","Even/Odd (Variante)","Sandwich (Variante)"],"links":[{"url":"https://tinyurl.com/n5j9p9y7","kind":"short"},{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/cvttdov16u","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://f-puzzles.com/?","linkKind":"short","summary":{"format":"fpuzzles","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":0,"hasSolution":false,"features":["odd","even","text","line","cage"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-04T23:44:39+00:00"}